        "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
        "revision": 1173695647,
        "heading": "Cultivation",
        "text": "This and other species in the genus, such as Blyxa japonica, are sold commercially as greenery to grow alongside fish in aquaria. They require moderate or bright light. Blyxa aubertii has been in the aquarium trade for a long time but has never been very popular.",
